A||||6||MooCow||How to install neons??||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||09-07-2001||09:11 PM||||I have the complete set of the street glow neons for under the car.  I have them all hooked up and they are not insight at all.  The thing is that I attached them with zip ties on the sides and they are holding just fine.  My worry is that I attached them to the metal tube lines that run on each side of the car, and thye get hott.  The neons are not getting hot, but the zip ties are.  So what else can I use to keep them up besides plastic cause it may melt.  I need to fix this before I leave tomorrow for Fierorama or I may show uo a little burnt.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-07-2001||09:42 PM||||Maybe you can screw electrical conduit clips(whatever they're called) somewhere...take a look in your basement or garage.  They're half round and come in all sorts of sizes.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||09-07-2001||11:01 PM||||Hose clamps maybe?<BR>What color did you get?||||reg||1
Z||000003||MooCow||09-08-2001||12:05 AM||||I ended up buying red ones cause my car is yellow.  Also I re did my interior with some red in it and it looks very sharp.  Well Im nerly off to Fierorama so I guess I will just use some wire for now till I get back or I'll just un hook them.  The give me plastic clips but no room for them on the sides so I used zip ties.  Also what are those 2 pipes that run on the side of the car??<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||09-08-2001||12:29 AM||||Those are your coolant send/return lines, so they will get hot very quickly.  You should go to menards and get some "plumber's strap", its a roll of bendable aluminum that has a lot of pre punched holes in it, so you can wrap that around the neons and then around the coolant tube, and hold it together with a 1/4-20 nut and bolt.  I know we got the stuff here at ace.||||reg||1
Z||000005||jch82||09-08-2001||02:20 AM||||What would we do without Joe??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Such a smart guy!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82(sig).jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000006||artherd||09-08-2001||05:24 AM||||Metal hose clamps should work, BUT... the coolant lines shouldn't get above 220-230f *ever* and this should be ok...<P>Still I'd feel better with Stainless hose clamps (be sure to get stainless entirely, incuding the screw.)<P>Neon's not my thing, but if it floats your boat, go for it!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
